Subject: [PATCH] feat(backend): project foundation - env settings, Supabase
 JWT auth, tooling, tests

- Settings read everything from environment variables (no secrets in Git); fail loudly if missing.
- PostgreSQL via DATABASE_URL (Supabase session pooler or direct connection).
- Verify Supabase access tokens with the project's public keys (JWKS): ES256/RS256 only,
  audience/issuer/expiry checked, anonymous users and non-'authenticated' roles refused.
- API closed by default (IsAuthenticated); public GET /api/health/, authenticated GET /api/me/.
- Tooling: pytest, ruff, strict mypy; pinned requirements (each pin >= 14 days old).
- 65 tests (token attacks, key-server outage, env parsing, defaults).

No database tables yet. Nothing outside Qeeva-Backend is changed.

